  "description": "Preview. Experimental. Decodes image files and streams (PNG and JPEG experimental; GIF, BMP and WebP untested) with SkiaSharp into Starlings.Models.EmbeddingGemma2 images, reproducing PIL's convert(\"RGB\") as the upstream processor sees it: alpha dropped (not composited), grayscale and palettes expanded, CMYK converted, no colour management, EXIF orientation ignored unless explicitly applied (a documented deviation from upstream). Images with 16 bits per channel are rejected (upstream saturates them to white). Decoded size limit 50 megapixels by default. Brings SkiaSharp (MIT) and its Linux natives (SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux.NoDependencies), whose bundled third-party notices include an MPL-1.1 GIF decoder and the Adobe DNG SDK license.",
